messages.content:
THOUGHT: NullAway is complaining that the builder’s @NonNull fields are not guaranteed to be initialized in the constructor. The simplest fix is to initialize them to safe non-null defaults in the private constructor. I’ll edit the file to set those fields to default values, then run the prescribed Gradle command to verify the error is gone.

```bash
cd /home/joos/projects/nullrepair/nullness-benchmarks/eureka && sed -i '113s/private ReplicationInstanceBuilder() {}/private ReplicationInstanceBuilder() {
      this.appName = "";
      this.id = "";
      this.lastDirtyTimestamp = 0L;
      this.instanceInfo = InstanceInfo.Builder.newBuilder().setAppName("").setVIPAddress("").build();
      this.action = Action.Heartbeat;
    }/' eureka-core/src/main/java/com/netflix/eureka/cluster/protocol/ReplicationInstance.java && nl -ba eureka-core/src/main/java/com/netflix/eureka/cluster/protocol/ReplicationInstance.java | sed -n '100,150p' && ./gradlew eureka-core:compileJava -x test -q > build_output.log 2>&1 || grep -A 5 -B 5 'ReplicationInstance.java' build_output.log
```

